1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:02,240
[Previously]
The feud between the two families

2
00:00:02,443 --> 00:00:05,600
started with Wirat and Sirin, your mother.

3
00:00:06,214 --> 00:00:08,840
We're going to run away together.

4
00:00:08,939 --> 00:00:11,280
And Yi really knows about this, right?

5
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:14,328
He already promised Tokyo he'd help us.

6
00:00:14,352 --> 00:00:16,680
You've got me. What are you scared of?

7
00:00:17,408 --> 00:00:19,080
Tell me how my dad died.

8
00:00:20,726 --> 00:00:22,320
But Yi's really coming, right?

9
00:00:23,211 --> 00:00:24,880
Yi would never break his promise to us.

10
00:00:30,576 --> 00:00:35,400
I confess to almighty God

11
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:37,142
and to you, my brothers and sisters,

12
00:00:38,107 --> 00:00:41,760
that I have greatly sinned

13
00:00:42,990 --> 00:00:46,920
in my thoughts and in my words,

14
00:00:48,552 --> 00:00:50,512
in what I have done and
what I have failed to do.

15
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:54,680
I have sinned.

16
00:00:57,363 --> 00:00:58,760
I admit

17
00:00:59,283 --> 00:01:00,284
that I am a sinner.

18
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,000
"Juliet &amp; Juliet" (Episode 7)

19
00:01:11,622 --> 00:01:13,720
Dad! Dad!

20
00:01:14,710 --> 00:01:15,880
What happened?

21
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:18,580
I've sent my men to look for them.

22
00:01:22,048 --> 00:01:23,049
Look for who, Big?

23
00:01:25,049 --> 00:01:26,050
Who did this to Yi?

24
00:01:35,936 --> 00:01:38,576
Doctor, how is my son?

25
00:01:48,123 --> 00:01:49,163
That's our rule, remember?

26
00:01:49,568 --> 00:01:51,210
Secret for secret.

27
00:01:52,192 --> 00:01:53,600
Next time, just tell me.

28
00:01:54,331 --> 00:01:56,250
It'll be our little
secret. I won't tell Dad.

29
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:04,020
Do you really want to go abroad that badly?

30
00:02:07,158 --> 00:02:08,159
Fine.

31
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:09,631
I'll talk to Dad for you.

32
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:12,520
- You will?
- Yeah.

33
00:02:13,174 --> 00:02:15,160
Make sure you find out what your dream is.

34
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,520
And stop thinking I'm so mean.

35
00:02:19,104 --> 00:02:21,184
I love you more than
anyone in this family, dumbass.

36
00:02:22,438 --> 00:02:25,310
I think you and your girlfriend should
get out of this town as soon as you can.

37
00:02:25,334 --> 00:02:28,294
I have a feeling our family and
theirs are going to clash sooner or later.

38
00:02:28,638 --> 00:02:31,318
And I don't want you getting caught up
in this because of me again.

39
00:02:32,248 --> 00:02:35,040
You've got me. What are you scared of?

40
00:02:45,139 --> 00:02:46,360
What do you mean, Doctor?

41
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:51,100
Go get the best doctor you
can find to save my child!

42
00:02:51,416 --> 00:02:52,417
Go!

43
00:02:52,579 --> 00:02:54,894
Yi has lost a lot of blood.

44
00:02:56,691 --> 00:02:58,560
What kind of blood do you need, huh?

45
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:02,080
Take Big's blood! Take all of his blood!

46
00:03:02,163 --> 00:03:03,164
Just take it!

47
00:03:04,050 --> 00:03:06,880
- Hurry! Take it!
- There's nothing more we can do.

48
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:09,440
Yi has passed away.

49
00:03:15,536 --> 00:03:16,600
Don't you dare tell me

50
00:03:17,414 --> 00:03:19,100
that my son is dead.

51
00:03:20,027 --> 00:03:21,360
Don't you fucking dare say that!

52
00:03:21,544 --> 00:03:23,480
You bastard! Don't you dare say it!

53
00:03:30,528 --> 00:03:32,040
Get up, it's okay.

54
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:13,100
Why the hell are you doing this?

55
00:04:16,811 --> 00:04:18,160
Yi killed my dad.

56
00:04:29,635 --> 00:04:32,350
I asked her to help Phu
with the insurance paperwork.

57
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,720
She gets a little extra for helping out.

58
00:06:01,982 --> 00:06:03,102
Are you ready, honey?

59
00:06:03,288 --> 00:06:05,160
Pakkard, you have to leave right now.

60
00:06:06,568 --> 00:06:08,392
- Pakkard, honey!
- Where is she going, Mom?

61
00:06:10,175 --> 00:06:12,606
Anywhere. She just needs
to get as far away as possible.

62
00:06:12,886 --> 00:06:14,280
She can even leave the province.

63
00:06:16,288 --> 00:06:17,448
Pakkard, are you okay, honey?

64
00:06:18,054 --> 00:06:19,960
Go on. Trust me, honey.

65
00:06:27,187 --> 00:06:28,360
I'm sorry, Blue.

66
00:06:31,094 --> 00:06:32,300
But I've already done it.

67
00:06:37,472 --> 00:06:38,473
Please, this way.

68
00:06:56,896 --> 00:06:58,480
Dad, was Pakkard telling the truth?

69
00:07:00,347 --> 00:07:01,960
Did Yi really kill Uncle Wirat?

70
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,801
Yes.

71
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,640
Then why did you tell Pakkard about it?

72
00:07:17,582 --> 00:07:18,960
You were trying to trick her...

73
00:07:20,276 --> 00:07:24,120
You used her to settle that stupid feud
between our families, didn't you?

74
00:07:26,211 --> 00:07:28,812
You said she was like
another daughter to you!

75
00:07:29,704 --> 00:07:31,735
How could you do this to her?

76
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:37,320
You're my only child.

77
00:07:41,523 --> 00:07:43,880
I know you're not exactly
a good person, Dad.

78
00:07:47,376 --> 00:07:49,424
But how can you be such an asshole?

79
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,507
Why should I keep it from her?

80
00:07:55,856 --> 00:07:56,857
Sooner or later,

81
00:07:57,456 --> 00:07:59,157
Pakkard would've found out anyway.

82
00:07:59,984 --> 00:08:01,307
I just told her the truth.

83
00:08:02,048 --> 00:08:03,049
As for everything else,

84
00:08:04,214 --> 00:08:06,480
Pakkard made her own decisions.

85
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:10,480
Are you sure you told her the truth, Dad?

86
00:08:14,472 --> 00:08:17,742
So I guess this gun just magically
appeared out of nowhere, huh?

87
00:08:25,163 --> 00:08:27,947
Everything has already been decided.

88
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:46,760
You just have to play your part.

89
00:09:16,083 --> 00:09:17,400
You killed my son!

90
00:09:18,350 --> 00:09:19,351
You fucking bitch!

91
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,200
You killed my child!

92
00:09:28,179 --> 00:09:29,180
Big!

93
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:31,801
Who killed Yi?

94
00:09:32,548 --> 00:09:33,549
Someone from that family.

95
00:09:34,371 --> 00:09:35,372
That bitch Pakkard.

96
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:42,240
Go wipe out her entire family!

97
00:09:43,784 --> 00:09:46,240
Your stupid family feud

98
00:09:47,192 --> 00:09:49,113
has already cost Yi his life!

99
00:09:50,318 --> 00:09:51,360
Stop it, Tokyo!

100
00:09:53,534 --> 00:09:54,535
No, I won't!

101
00:09:54,947 --> 00:09:56,760
You and Dad are the ones who need to stop!

102
00:09:58,291 --> 00:09:59,292
I know what happened

103
00:10:00,414 --> 00:10:01,920
17 years ago.

104
00:10:02,766 --> 00:10:04,120
Pakkard's father died

105
00:10:04,995 --> 00:10:07,400
because you ordered
Yi to kill him, didn't you?

106
00:10:09,091 --> 00:10:11,520
This is exactly why! You
keep killing each other!

107
00:10:12,595 --> 00:10:14,480
That's why this will never end, Dad!

108
00:10:15,102 --> 00:10:17,280
You kill one of them,
and they kill one of us!

109
00:10:17,303 --> 00:10:19,263
Stop talking about things
you know nothing about!

110
00:10:21,264 --> 00:10:22,265
What don't I know?

111
00:10:24,243 --> 00:10:26,403
If you think I don't know,
then tell me the truth!

112
00:10:26,616 --> 00:10:27,920
Yi acted on her own.

113
00:10:31,198 --> 00:10:32,840
Nobody wanted any of this to happen!

114
00:10:35,532 --> 00:10:36,880
Yi did it on his own!

115
00:10:38,667 --> 00:10:40,467
No one in this family
knew anything about it!

116
00:10:45,619 --> 00:10:47,680
But you helped Yi cover
up what he did, didn't you?

117
00:10:50,656 --> 00:10:52,256
Did you want your brother to go to jail?

118
00:10:54,712 --> 00:10:56,472
Do you want everyone
in the province to know

119
00:10:58,030 --> 00:10:59,670
that our family is full of murderers?

120
00:11:04,584 --> 00:11:06,500
I've done the best I could, Tokyo.

121
00:11:08,104 --> 00:11:10,600
Yi did what he thought was right, too.

122
00:11:12,979 --> 00:11:14,659
What the hell was right about any of this?

123
00:11:18,485 --> 00:11:20,486
Yi ended up dead because of it!

124
00:11:25,627 --> 00:11:26,628
Dad!

125
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,880
How many more people have to die

126
00:11:30,224 --> 00:11:31,560
before this finally ends?

127
00:11:34,315 --> 00:11:35,316
Dad,

128
00:11:36,848 --> 00:11:39,360
let's do the right thing. Please.

129
00:11:41,750 --> 00:11:42,751
The right thing?

130
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:46,680
What exactly is the right thing?

131
00:11:50,739 --> 00:11:52,200
You're so selfish

132
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:55,500
that you can't even see the truth.

133
00:12:01,310 --> 00:12:03,180
That bastard Wirat deceived your mother.

134
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:09,960
Then he planted a bomb
in her car and killed her.

135
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,741
[Wirat: Sirin, see you at four.]

136
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,121
[Po]

137
00:12:57,776 --> 00:12:59,376
You're planning to run away, aren't you?

138
00:12:59,702 --> 00:13:01,856
You're still thinking of
leaving with that bastard Wirat?

139
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:03,960
The Monchaikul family is deceiving you!

140
00:13:05,046 --> 00:13:06,320
Just let me go.

141
00:13:06,774 --> 00:13:09,782
Sirin, you are not taking Tokyo anywhere!

142
00:13:38,502 --> 00:13:39,880
Tokyo, sweetheart.

143
00:13:40,331 --> 00:13:42,160
Come start a new life
with Mommy, sweetheart.

144
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:43,701
Okay?

145
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:45,991
Uncle Wirat will pick us up soon.

146
00:14:08,184 --> 00:14:09,185
Sirin!

147
00:14:12,766 --> 00:14:13,767
Tokyo!

148
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,321
Tokyo!

149
00:14:44,224 --> 00:14:45,225
As for you,

150
00:14:46,619 --> 00:14:47,880
you're lucky

151
00:14:49,822 --> 00:14:52,000
you survived to stand here and insult me!

152
00:14:57,870 --> 00:14:59,920
I never wanted you to know the whole truth.

153
00:15:01,915 --> 00:15:02,916
But in the end,

154
00:15:03,675 --> 00:15:06,680
raising you without telling you anything

155
00:15:06,971 --> 00:15:08,720
only made you more stubborn

156
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,254
and left you vulnerable to their lies!

157
00:15:13,248 --> 00:15:14,560
Do you still love her?

158
00:15:16,230 --> 00:15:18,680
Even though her family

159
00:15:19,323 --> 00:15:20,923
killed your mother with their own hands?

160
00:15:23,781 --> 00:15:26,640
Do you still believe in
your pure, innocent love?

161
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:30,400
Or do you think your love

162
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:34,840
can somehow wash away your mother's blood
that was spilled all those years ago?

163
00:15:35,321 --> 00:15:36,322
Huh?

164
00:15:42,330 --> 00:15:45,320
Yi may have been wrong

165
00:15:46,270 --> 00:15:47,640
to kill someone,

166
00:15:48,944 --> 00:15:50,250
but he did the right thing

167
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:54,000
by avenging your mother's death.

168
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:46,840
What more do you want?

169
00:16:56,592 --> 00:17:00,400
I don't have a secret
room like you and Yi did.

170
00:17:03,747 --> 00:17:05,000
So I had to come here.

171
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:09,680
There's something I
want to talk to you about.

172
00:17:14,688 --> 00:17:16,728
I've been through what
you're going through, Tokyo.

173
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:22,520
I was young once, too.

174
00:17:25,576 --> 00:17:26,800
I wanted to rebel.

175
00:17:28,936 --> 00:17:31,760
I used to long for the
day Dad would accept me

176
00:17:33,107 --> 00:17:34,208
more than he accepted Yi.

177
00:17:55,830 --> 00:17:57,640
That desire to be loved,

178
00:17:59,814 --> 00:18:01,880
loving someone with all your heart,

179
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,320
I've felt those things, too.

180
00:18:11,830 --> 00:18:12,840
But the older I get,

181
00:18:14,571 --> 00:18:17,480
the more I realize those
feelings don't last forever.

182
00:18:22,570 --> 00:18:24,450
What's more important than love

183
00:18:27,504 --> 00:18:28,760
is responsibility.

184
00:18:55,179 --> 00:18:56,819
There are many paths we can take in life.

185
00:19:02,048 --> 00:19:03,049
But I know

186
00:19:04,971 --> 00:19:07,110
my little sister will
make the right choice.

187
00:20:14,030 --> 00:20:16,080
You've heard what happened, haven't you?

188
00:20:34,707 --> 00:20:35,708
I'm sorry.

189
00:20:45,587 --> 00:20:47,160
What are you apologizing for?

190
00:20:51,341 --> 00:20:53,280
I'm apologizing on Pakkard's behalf.

191
00:20:55,992 --> 00:20:59,640
I know I shouldn't say this, but I...

192
00:21:01,107 --> 00:21:02,900
Can we please not talk
about this right now?

193
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:13,601
I know

194
00:21:14,936 --> 00:21:16,700
you don't want me to be angry with Pakkard.

195
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:21,150
I can't tell you how to feel.

196
00:21:23,763 --> 00:21:25,360
What happened was too serious.

197
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:28,840
You can be angry or furious.

198
00:21:29,208 --> 00:21:31,309
You have every right to
feel however you want.

199
00:21:32,227 --> 00:21:33,960
I won't hold any of that against you.

200
00:21:36,339 --> 00:21:37,340
It's just that...

201
00:21:39,726 --> 00:21:42,880
I want you to know that between us,

202
00:21:45,195 --> 00:21:46,600
nothing has changed.

203
00:21:53,643 --> 00:21:55,720
I'm just not ready to
talk about this right now.

204
00:22:08,646 --> 00:22:11,000
My family is looking for Pakkard right now.

205
00:22:14,248 --> 00:22:15,720
Pakkard isn't here anymore.

206
00:22:16,387 --> 00:22:19,320
My parents helped her escape to the border.

207
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:22,300
I don't know how she's doing now.

208
00:22:25,795 --> 00:22:27,880
So you helped Pakkard escape, too?

209
00:22:34,531 --> 00:22:35,532
I...

210
00:22:50,016 --> 00:22:52,758
Pakkard killed my brother Yi!

211
00:22:57,899 --> 00:23:00,400
Didn't you say people who
do wrong should be punished?

212
00:23:04,987 --> 00:23:06,680
Or is it because she's your friend?

213
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:09,240
So you're just going to let it slide?

214
00:23:14,075 --> 00:23:17,076
What happened to all that
justice you've been fighting for?

215
00:23:23,600 --> 00:23:26,320
But Yi killed Pakkard's father!

216
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:33,600
So that gives her the right
to kill him for revenge?

217
00:24:23,795 --> 00:24:24,796
I'm sorry.

218
00:24:26,700 --> 00:24:27,701
I'm sorry.

219
00:24:38,875 --> 00:24:40,120
We won't repeat

220
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:45,440
the same mistakes our
parents made, will we?

221
00:25:03,768 --> 00:25:05,900
What's going to happen to us now?

222
00:26:02,979 --> 00:26:04,400
Who do you think killed Yi?

223
00:26:05,374 --> 00:26:08,194
I don't know. But with
the kind of life Yi led,

224
00:26:08,250 --> 00:26:09,880
it was bound to happen sooner or later.

225
00:26:10,568 --> 00:26:13,080
My mom said people at
the market are gossiping

226
00:26:13,100 --> 00:26:14,540
that Pakkard was the one who did it.

227
00:26:14,765 --> 00:26:17,000
Hey, and what about that rumor

228
00:26:17,246 --> 00:26:19,800
that Tokyo and Blue are dating? Is it true?

229
00:26:24,792 --> 00:26:26,432
What the fuck are you guys talking about?

230
00:26:46,240 --> 00:26:47,241
Are you okay?

231
00:26:49,790 --> 00:26:51,670
Why the hell does everyone
keep asking me that?

232
00:26:54,291 --> 00:26:55,440
Am I okay or not?

233
00:26:57,760 --> 00:26:59,761
Try going through what I've been through!

234
00:27:01,115 --> 00:27:03,120
Let's see if you can still say you're okay!

235
00:27:08,184 --> 00:27:09,600
We're just worried about you.

236
00:27:15,272 --> 00:27:16,273
Hey...

237
00:27:19,862 --> 00:27:20,960
I'm sorry.

238
00:27:28,160 --> 00:27:29,240
It's okay.

239
00:27:31,220 --> 00:27:32,640
Actually, I think...

240
00:27:34,150 --> 00:27:36,120
if you had to choose who to believe,

241
00:27:39,635 --> 00:27:41,395
Jai would be more
believable than me anyway.

242
00:27:49,950 --> 00:27:51,750
But I still owe you an apology.

243
00:27:57,603 --> 00:27:59,000
I'm really sorry.

244
00:28:11,780 --> 00:28:12,781
Someday,

245
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:16,301
when I'm no longer around,

246
00:28:19,403 --> 00:28:21,120
you should have a proper talk with Jai.

247
00:29:02,614 --> 00:29:04,134
I was the one who started all of this.

248
00:29:05,408 --> 00:29:08,240
So I'll take responsibility
for everything I've done.

249
00:29:14,984 --> 00:29:17,680
My little sister shouldn't
have to inherit this hatred.

250
00:29:19,528 --> 00:29:22,250
Tokyo deserves to live the life she wants.

251
00:30:15,080 --> 00:30:17,081
[The direct admission results are out.]

252
00:30:26,040 --> 00:30:28,200
[List of Students Admitted
to Srisilapasat University]

253
00:30:32,520 --> 00:30:34,521
[Phakjira Monchaitrakul]

254
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:47,720
Sinittha... Sinittha Kongpurim.

255
00:31:23,568 --> 00:31:24,569
Congratulations

256
00:31:25,720 --> 00:31:27,520
on getting accepted
through direct admission.

257
00:31:29,534 --> 00:31:30,535
Thanks.

258
00:31:32,200 --> 00:31:33,201
Yeah.

259
00:31:35,027 --> 00:31:36,984
But your name...

260
00:31:37,790 --> 00:31:38,791
Yeah.

261
00:31:40,136 --> 00:31:41,376
I couldn't find it on the list.

262
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:44,301
Guess I didn't get in this time.

263
00:31:48,500 --> 00:31:49,501
Hey!

264
00:31:51,350 --> 00:31:52,351
It's okay.

265
00:31:53,483 --> 00:31:54,800
I can go somewhere else.

266
00:31:57,027 --> 00:31:58,750
Maybe a private university in Bangkok.

267
00:31:59,475 --> 00:32:00,760
There are plenty of good ones.

268
00:32:09,078 --> 00:32:10,760
Are you sure your dad won't mind?

269
00:32:14,480 --> 00:32:15,600
I don't care anymore.

270
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:28,822
Hello? Where the hell are you?

271
00:32:29,264 --> 00:32:30,320
I'm at the border.

272
00:32:30,939 --> 00:32:33,600
Once it gets dark, I have
to cross over into Myanmar.

273
00:32:34,043 --> 00:32:35,718
I probably won't be able to
contact you for a long time.

274
00:32:35,742 --> 00:32:37,222
So I wanted to call and let you know.

275
00:32:41,011 --> 00:32:44,280
Don't worry about me.
Just focus on keeping yourself safe, okay?

276
00:32:44,670 --> 00:32:46,056
Once you make it across,

277
00:32:46,100 --> 00:32:47,920
just call me when you're safe.

278
00:32:48,910 --> 00:32:51,064
Yeah. Thanks so much.

279
00:32:51,416 --> 00:32:52,880
I'm really sorry, Blue.

280
00:33:00,342 --> 00:33:01,343
Are you leaving?

281
00:33:02,379 --> 00:33:03,380
Yeah.

282
00:33:04,918 --> 00:33:07,800
I have to help with Yi's
funeral arrangements tonight.

283
00:33:11,302 --> 00:33:14,560
Besides, I don't want any
more trouble right now.

284
00:33:19,230 --> 00:33:20,231
I should get going.

285
00:33:43,419 --> 00:33:45,779
[Lanna Sirin Kongpurin
March 11, 1972 - October 30, 2009]

286
00:33:52,592 --> 00:33:55,147
I don't know why she did it,

287
00:33:55,959 --> 00:34:00,180
but I can assure you that I absolutely
do not condone my niece's actions.

288
00:34:00,674 --> 00:34:04,250
And where is Pakkard now?

289
00:34:05,880 --> 00:34:06,881
I don't know.

290
00:34:07,614 --> 00:34:08,615
Are you sure?

291
00:34:10,104 --> 00:34:13,704
It's hard to believe one girl could pull off
such a brazen attack on the Kongpurim family.

292
00:34:13,939 --> 00:34:15,320
I find that highly unlikely.

293
00:34:17,853 --> 00:34:19,380
Anything is possible, Inspector.

294
00:34:20,398 --> 00:34:22,350
They hurt us, we hurt them.

295
00:34:23,475 --> 00:34:24,480
You know as well as I do

296
00:34:25,059 --> 00:34:26,900
that this cycle has
been going on for years.

297
00:34:29,422 --> 00:34:30,640
Anyway, this time,

298
00:34:31,480 --> 00:34:34,500
I'll cooperate fully
with your investigation.

299
00:34:35,373 --> 00:34:38,360
After all, whoever is
guilty must be punished.

300
00:34:41,432 --> 00:34:44,240
If anything happens to
my niece in the future,

301
00:34:45,363 --> 00:34:48,520
I hope you'll hold the
Kongpurim family accountable

302
00:34:48,907 --> 00:34:50,440
to the same standards.

303
00:35:29,336 --> 00:35:30,337
Honey!

304
00:35:30,632 --> 00:35:32,072
Send someone to help Pakkard! Hurry!

305
00:35:32,542 --> 00:35:34,360
They've found Pakkard!

306
00:35:37,150 --> 00:35:38,151
Mom!

307
00:35:39,278 --> 00:35:42,149
Didn't Pakkard tell me
she was fleeing the country?

308
00:35:42,432 --> 00:35:45,280
I don't know how they
found our safe house!

309
00:35:45,547 --> 00:35:47,760
Maybe one of our men let it slip.

310
00:35:50,760 --> 00:35:53,160
Honey, please! Do something!

311
00:35:53,347 --> 00:35:55,147
Are you just going to
let your own niece die?

312
00:35:56,355 --> 00:35:57,800
Whatever happens, happens.

313
00:35:59,156 --> 00:36:01,560
But if she really does die, all the better.

314
00:36:04,080 --> 00:36:05,960
Then taking revenge on the Kongpurim family

315
00:36:06,861 --> 00:36:08,762
will be justified in
the eyes of our family.

316
00:36:12,700 --> 00:36:13,701
You fucking...

317
00:36:50,520 --> 00:36:52,621
Did you tell your family
where Pakkard was hiding?

318
00:37:05,267 --> 00:37:07,168
Pakkard really did kill Yi.

319
00:37:10,603 --> 00:37:12,563
She has to face the
consequences of what she did.

320
00:37:17,963 --> 00:37:19,360
I never should've trusted you.

321
00:37:43,291 --> 00:37:46,120
Didn't you say our families
couldn't tear us apart?

322
00:37:47,883 --> 00:37:48,884
Huh?

323
00:37:51,131 --> 00:37:54,480
Didn't you say they couldn't hurt us?

324
00:38:00,563 --> 00:38:02,400
But we can't move
forward like this, either!

325
00:38:04,152 --> 00:38:06,200
What? Move forward with what?

326
00:38:07,475 --> 00:38:10,160
The past is still unresolved!
Things still haven't been made right!

327
00:38:10,176 --> 00:38:11,280
We can't move forward.

328
00:38:14,901 --> 00:38:16,500
You might not know this,

329
00:38:18,200 --> 00:38:20,101
but the reason Yi killed Wirat

330
00:38:22,019 --> 00:38:23,880
was because he murdered my mother!

331
00:38:26,664 --> 00:38:27,680
What do you mean?

332
00:38:31,320 --> 00:38:34,640
Your uncle was the one
who started all of this.

333
00:38:40,456 --> 00:38:42,680
If you're saying Pakkard had her reasons,

334
00:38:45,163 --> 00:38:46,640
then so did my brother.

335
00:38:59,020 --> 00:39:01,560
I was foolish enough to think
you were different from them.

336
00:39:04,627 --> 00:39:07,267
But you know what? You're becoming
the kind of adult we both hate.

337
00:39:13,900 --> 00:39:16,220
If you choose to be like the
rest of the Kongpurim family,

338
00:39:21,401 --> 00:39:22,761
then don't ever come see me again.

339
00:39:31,280 --> 00:39:32,650
What are you two doing here?

340
00:39:39,832 --> 00:39:41,700
It's not like I want to be here, either.

341
00:39:42,664 --> 00:39:43,665
Excuse me.

342
00:39:43,827 --> 00:39:46,400
Things might not be as you think.

343
00:39:50,435 --> 00:39:51,920
I guess it's time

344
00:39:52,152 --> 00:39:53,880
I told you the truth

345
00:39:54,320 --> 00:39:55,651
about how all of this started.

346
00:39:56,408 --> 00:39:57,409
It all began with love.

347
00:40:10,232 --> 00:40:11,920
17 years ago,

348
00:40:12,344 --> 00:40:16,000
the two families were fiercely
competing for a port concession.

349
00:40:16,760 --> 00:40:19,600
A worker from the Monchaikul
family was shot dead,

350
00:40:20,091 --> 00:40:21,880
and no one knew who was responsible.

351
00:40:22,971 --> 00:40:23,972
What should we do, boss?

352
00:40:24,624 --> 00:40:25,625
Listen.

353
00:40:26,091 --> 00:40:29,720
Call that military officer you know and
have him deal with those damn Kongpurims!

354
00:40:30,374 --> 00:40:32,320
We can't just let our men die like this!

355
00:40:33,480 --> 00:40:35,640
Take care of it quietly.

356
00:40:35,877 --> 00:40:37,960
Don't let it affect the port concession.

357
00:40:41,179 --> 00:40:42,360
Stay out of this.

358
00:40:43,854 --> 00:40:45,486
Is this why

359
00:40:46,179 --> 00:40:47,419
you won't go after that family?

360
00:40:47,918 --> 00:40:51,240
Wiboon believed Wirat was
going soft because of his love

361
00:40:51,374 --> 00:40:54,560
for his first love, Sirin, Tokyo's mother.

362
00:40:55,125 --> 00:40:57,200
Come on, be realistic!

363
00:40:57,350 --> 00:41:00,406
You have a child, and she
has a family of her own!

364
00:41:00,619 --> 00:41:03,040
Why the hell are you still
hung up on your first love? Huh?

365
00:41:03,462 --> 00:41:05,680
- Face reality!
- Yeah, I get it!

366
00:41:08,264 --> 00:41:10,040
Just do as I say.

367
00:41:10,963 --> 00:41:11,964
Stay out of it.

368
00:41:16,416 --> 00:41:20,800
Wiboon still wanted his brother
to lead the family business.

369
00:41:29,360 --> 00:41:32,120
My brother was blinded by love

370
00:41:32,832 --> 00:41:35,440
and was ready to abandon
everything our family had built

371
00:41:36,272 --> 00:41:37,720
to start a new life.

372
00:41:38,518 --> 00:41:41,360
He had no idea that his actions

373
00:41:41,856 --> 00:41:44,040
would make everything
our family had worked for

374
00:41:44,720 --> 00:41:45,800
go to waste.

375
00:41:46,700 --> 00:41:48,020
So what are you going to do, son?

376
00:41:49,363 --> 00:41:50,364
I'll do

377
00:41:51,523 --> 00:41:52,880
what I have to do.

378
00:41:57,752 --> 00:42:00,050
Wiboon was the mastermind behind it all.

379
00:42:01,753 --> 00:42:03,360
He made Mr. Po believe

380
00:42:03,490 --> 00:42:06,400
that Wirat had plotted to
deceive Sirin and kill her.

381
00:42:16,502 --> 00:42:17,503
Sirin!

382
00:42:22,992 --> 00:42:23,993
Yeah.

383
00:42:25,166 --> 00:42:29,120
And that was the beginning
of an endless cycle of revenge.

384
00:43:10,790 --> 00:43:12,320
Sometimes, the truth hurts.

385
00:43:13,867 --> 00:43:15,734
But if we refuse to accept it,

386
00:43:16,411 --> 00:43:18,250
we'll never be able to make things right.

387
00:43:29,707 --> 00:43:31,440
What the father said makes sense.

388
00:43:36,587 --> 00:43:38,667
I guess there's really no
way to fix things anymore.

389
00:43:42,774 --> 00:43:43,880
Because the Kongpurim

390
00:43:45,419 --> 00:43:46,700
and Monchaikul families

391
00:43:48,480 --> 00:43:50,040
will never be able to reconcile.

392
00:44:23,808 --> 00:44:24,809
You bitch!

393
00:44:41,560 --> 00:44:44,040
[Next Episode Preview] After
everything I've done to raise you,

394
00:44:44,440 --> 00:44:46,846
is this how you repay me, huh?

395
00:44:47,360 --> 00:44:48,680
If you're going to shoot Pakkard,

396
00:44:49,189 --> 00:44:50,480
you'll have to kill me first.

397
00:44:51,335 --> 00:44:53,800
No matter who tells us what we should do,

398
00:44:53,840 --> 00:44:55,840
we're the ones who make
our own choices, right?

399
00:44:57,720 --> 00:44:59,160
I'm a Kongpurim,

400
00:44:59,824 --> 00:45:01,760
and you're a Monchaikul.

401
00:45:02,200 --> 00:45:03,560
But if I choose you,

402
00:45:04,059 --> 00:45:05,300
will you choose me?
